    "merge_review": {
      "proposals": [
        {
          "group_ids": [
            "hs.merge/H1",
            "hs.merge/H6"
          ],
          "reason": "The two groups describe the same coherent LRG/BGS absorption structure at essentially identical redshift (0.15896775 vs 0.15892043, Δz≈4.7e-5). The type-diagnostic Ca K and Ca H lines are matched to the same observed features: Ca K at 4561.006 Å and Ca H at 4601.599 Å in both groups, with the same measured Ca H/K separation (~40.59 Å) and the same Ca K/Ca H amplitude ratio (~0.943). Both have adopted Ca H/K pairs with FA doublet support (3/3 yes) and identical Dn4000 (1.53098). The G band, Mg I, Na D CWT feature, N II, and Si II pairs also coincide at the same observed wavelengths, and the shared cwt:abs:0000 TBD identity is common to both. The only differences are hypothesis-local fit IDs and sub-Å predicted offsets, which do not indicate independent observations. This is a single observed structure represented by two nearly identical hypotheses."
        }
      ],
      "reason": "H1 and H6 are credible duplicates: they share the same Ca K/Ca H diagnostic absorption doublet at the same observed wavelengths and separation, the same Dn4000, and the same set of supporting features (G band, Mg I, Na D CWT, N II, Si II). The redshift difference is tiny and the line identities are consistent, so they plausibly describe one coherent observed LRG/BGS structure rather than two independent ones."
    },
